{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01496",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.95,
      "end_seconds": 2.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "welcome. Make yourself comfortable"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.0,
      "end_seconds": 7.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Um, afternoon, is this seat fine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.27,
      "end_seconds": 9.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "What's been worrying you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.55,
      "end_seconds": 15.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "I wanted to get my heart racing looked at"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.28,
      "end_seconds": 19.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.48,
      "end_seconds": 31.99,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "It's been going on for about a month. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.24,
      "end_seconds": 41.14,
      "duration_seconds": 7.9,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.96,
      "end_seconds": 55.9,
      "duration_seconds": 13.94,
      "text": "it settles a little with lying down and slow breathing. About a four out of ten. It happens a couple of times a week. It's worse with coffee"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.44,
      "end_seconds": 59.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "So, does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.88,
      "end_seconds": 89.72,
      "duration_seconds": 27.84,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a fluttering in my chest as well. I mean, and I've been feeling anxious during it as well, for two months. With feeling anxious during it, I'd say mild. Ah, you know, the fluttering in my chest? That's been for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.43,
      "end_seconds": 103.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "alright, are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.42,
      "end_seconds": 112.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.23,
      "text": "sorry, um, what was I saying, I'm allergic to kiwi, I get hives"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.71,
      "end_seconds": 116.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.12,
      "end_seconds": 120.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Diabetes, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.35,
      "end_seconds": 131.42,
      "duration_seconds": 9.07,
      "text": "Right, so diabetes is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.71,
      "end_seconds": 139.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "I had a mole taken off my arm a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.64,
      "end_seconds": 159.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.67,
      "end_seconds": 167.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.57,
      "text": "I'm on something called glic... gliclazide, 80 milligrams, maybe, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.94,
      "end_seconds": 173.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.19,
      "end_seconds": 180.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Okay, so not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.66,
      "end_seconds": 184.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.02,
      "end_seconds": 200.23,
      "duration_seconds": 14.21,
      "text": "My partner and our baby. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.01,
      "end_seconds": 203.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Any chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.74,
      "end_seconds": 208.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Ah, not at all, no chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.14,
      "end_seconds": 214.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "A A few quick ones: sweating, tremor or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.35,
      "end_seconds": 219.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "so, no, no sweating, tremor or fainting"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.97,
      "end_seconds": 222.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.01,
      "end_seconds": 225.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 239.06,
      "end_seconds": 245.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse 113, blood pressure 128 over 70, saturation 98 percent"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.04,
      "end_seconds": 247.74,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.38,
      "end_seconds": 254.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.69,
      "end_seconds": 257.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.03,
      "end_seconds": 261.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "hold that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.65,
      "end_seconds": 276.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal with no murmur"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.31,
      "end_seconds": 280.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.62,
      "end_seconds": 299.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "The pulse is irregular, around ninety beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.01,
      "end_seconds": 314.74,
      "duration_seconds": 10.73,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Taking everything into account, the most likely explanation is paroxysmal palpitations, possibly an atrial arrhythmia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.03,
      "end_seconds": 317.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.89,
      "end_seconds": 353.06,
      "duration_seconds": 34.17,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like paroxysmal palpitations, possibly an atrial arrhythmia, but I'd like to confirm. Let's get a heart monitor for a few days, for palpitations. Let's get an ECG, for palpitations. I'm prescribing bisoprolol, 2.5 milligrams, once a day, until review. You take it by mouth. That should help with heart rate control. Cut right back on coffee, tea and energy drinks for now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.28,
      "end_seconds": 380.47,
      "duration_seconds": 23.19,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. One warning sign to remember: you faint or get chest pain with the racing. In that case don't wait. I'd like you back in three weeks. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.37,
      "end_seconds": 386.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "okay, that makes sense thanks for explaining"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.87,
      "end_seconds": 388.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}